Pages = {303-317},
Month = {SEP-DEC},
Abstract = {This study looks to investigate that other Environmental Learnings are
   possible from the pampeana music from Brazil and Uruguay. Based on the
   studies of Michael Foucault and authors from the education and
   environmental education in an post structutural perspective, the
   research contrasts the relationship between the music and the scenery of
   the Pampa. From two different aesthetic points of view. The cold
   aesthetic, the one of the musician Victor Ramil and the Uruguaian
   musicians Jorger Drexler and Daniel Drexler. Between these conceptual
   aesthetics there is a relationship between the music, the scenary of the
   Pampa, the places where the cold and temperate climate shapes one's way
   of being, of composing and becoming a subject. In that way, this study
   understands music as a strong cultural practice capable of contributing
   in the education process, and in the (trans)formations that happens
   between human relationships and nature, of the relationship with space,
   scenery, in the construction of different schools of thought in
   Education and Environmental Education.},
